  "notes": [
    "Events: all 5 bus events (project.added, snapshot.changed, run.finished, run.waiting, ticket.status-written) are emitted only from use cases. No emits outside use cases.",
    "Subscriptions: scheduler/api/subscriptions/subscribe-to-run-finished -> SettleFinishedRunUseCase; subscribe-to-run-waiting -> SettleWaitingRunUseCase; subscribe-to-snapshot-changed -> MergeApprovedPullRequestsUseCase. Wired in scheduler.start().",
    "Watcher subscriptions (subscribe-to-project-added, subscribe-to-ticket-status-written, subscribe-to-run-finished) do not call a use case directly: they call inline callbacks in watcher/index.ts that update in-memory state (watchRepository / recordStatusWrite) and call requestPoll() -> PollRepositoriesUseCase.execute. Event edges to watcher.uc.PollRepositoriesUseCase are therefore indirect.",
    "RecoverInterruptedRunsUseCase emits run.finished itself AND is given finishRun (FinishRunUseCase), which also emits run.finished.",
    "Every cross-module port is filled in main.ts by an inline lambda/object, not a direct method reference, except scheduler RunnerPort findRun/activeRuns/latestRun/settle/sessionLog (direct refs). RunnerPort.start/answer lambdas also translate runner errors to scheduler errors; runner.start is called with mode 'afk' added.",
    "bridge CheckpointAnswers.answer lambda -> scheduler.answer with {kind:'checkpoint', text}, maps scheduler errors to PageBusyError. bridge TicketRunLookup.latest -> runner.latestRun, late-bound (runner built after bridge).",
    "runner RunTargets.find lambda combines projects.list AND watcher.ticket (two calls edges).",
    "scheduler TicketLookup.find -> watcher.ticket (reshaped); ReviewedTicketLookup.list -> watcher.openTickets; RunsGate.check -> skills.runsBlocked; ProjectLookup.find -> projects.list (filtered). findings ProjectLookup.find -> projects.list (filtered).",
    "watcher ActiveRunLookup.activeRunTicketNumbers -> runner.activeRuns, late-bound (runner built after watcher).",
    "watcher RegisteredRepositories.list -> projects.list is used by watcher/index.ts start() directly, not by a use case. No edge added.",
    "runner appTools = [...findings.tools, ...bridge.tools] passed into LaunchRunSessionUseCase.tools. Modeled as 'tools' interface entries (properties, not methods) and calls edges via 'tools'. findings.tools wraps ReportFindingUseCase; bridge.tools wraps PublishArtifactUseCase. The agent session invokes them, not the use case code directly.",
    "RunnerPort calls edges list only the RunnerPort methods each use case actually calls, not all 7 methods.",
    "Interface methods without a use case: runner.abortSessions (agentSessions.stopAll inline), scheduler.start (wires subscriptions), skills.runsBlocked (domain fn determineRunsBlocked over cached state), watcher.stop, watcher.openTickets (reads in-memory snapshot).",
    "skills.start runs BOTH StartSkillsUseCase and ReadCredentialsUseCase; schema allows one, StartSkillsUseCase listed. watcher.start runs PollRepositoriesUseCase via requestPoll (also registers subscriptions).",
    "Routes/kitRoutes/pageRoutes properties excluded from interface. Use cases reached only via routes: bridge ListTicketArtifacts, ReadPage*, WritePageState, SubmitPageEvent; findings ListFindings, CreateTicketFromFinding, DismissFinding; projects AddProject; runner StopRun; scheduler StartTicketRun, ReadTicketRun, ResetTicket, ReadTicketSessionLog, AnswerRun (also interface). watcher.ReadProjectBoardUseCase via tickets routes.",
    "GhCliGitHubToken (port GitHubToken) is not used by any use case: injected into FetchIssueFeeds and FetchGraphQLTicketSource (infra -> infra). No edge.",
    "Shared adapters skipped: SystemClock, RandomUuidIdentifiers, TypedEventBus, logger. Non-class infra helpers skipped: runner map-sdk-message.ts, scheduler run-gh-command.ts, skills run-claude.ts, watcher request-github.ts.",
    "uses edges come from declared constructor dependencies; each declared dependency was checked to be referenced in its use case body."
  ]
